      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>mtu</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>integer</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>MTU is the maximum transmission unit for a network. MTU is optional, if not provided, the globally configured value in OVN-Kubernetes (defaults to 1400) is used for the network.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>role</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>Role describes the network role in the pod. Allowed values are "Primary" and "Secondary". Primary network is automatically assigned to every pod created in the same namespace. Secondary network is only assigned to pods that use <code>k8s.v1.cni.cncf.io/networks</code> annotation to select given network.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>subnets</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>array</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>Subnets are used for the pod network across the cluster. Dual-stack clusters may set 2 subnets (one for each IP family), otherwise only 1 subnet is allowed. Given subnet is split into smaller subnets for every node.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>subnets[]</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell></TableCell>
